## Question

Is tools/report.py's rounding of totals right for money, and what should change?

## Member 1: codex:gpt-6-astra · default

Status: answered · exit 0 · 31s · run codex-20261102-120000-aaaaa1 · 246 bytes

totals sums binary floating-point amounts and rounds once at the end. Use decimal.Decimal for money and explicitly choose ROUND_HALF_EVEN to reduce repeated tie bias. Parse prices directly from their strings. Test empty input and a half-cent tie.

## Member 2: claude:opus · default

Status: answered · exit 0 · 32s · run claude-20261102-120000-aaaaa2 · 282 bytes

totals sums floats and rounds once at the end. Money should use decimal.Decimal. I recommend ROUND_HALF_UP to match the stated customer-facing convention, but confirm that convention. Update compute_totals to quantize cents. Decide whether to round each order or only the final sum.

